# 2025星火英语高考词汇
# 领域: 高考
# 学科: 英语
# 来源: 2025星火英语·高考词汇
# 描述: 2025星火英语高考核心词汇精讲

{{abandon /əˈbændən/}}{{v. 放弃；遗弃。搭配：abandon oneself to（沉溺于）。例句：Never abandon hope, even in the darkest times.（即使在最黑暗的时刻也不要放弃希望。）派生：abandonment n.}}

{{absorb /əbˈsɔːb/}}{{v. 吸收；使全神贯注。搭配：be absorbed in（全神贯注于）。例句：She was so absorbed in her book that she forgot to eat.（她看书太入迷，忘了吃饭。）派生：absorption n., absorbing adj.}}

{{access /ˈækses/}}{{n. 进入；通道；使用权。搭配：have access to（有权使用）。例句：Every student should have access to quality education.（每个学生都应该有权获得优质教育。）派生：accessible adj.}}

{{accommodate /əˈkɒmədeɪt/}}{{v. 容纳；提供住宿；适应。搭配：accommodate oneself to（适应）。例句：The hotel can accommodate 200 guests.（酒店可容纳200位客人。）派生：accommodation n.}}

{{accomplish /əˈkʌmplɪʃ/}}{{v. 完成；实现。搭配：accomplish a goal/task（完成目标/任务）。例句：She accomplished her dream of becoming a doctor.（她实现了成为医生的梦想。）派生：accomplishment n.}}

{{accurate /ˈækjərət/}}{{adj. 准确的；精确的。搭配：be accurate in（在…方面准确）。例句：The report provides an accurate picture of the situation.（报告准确地描绘了情况。）派生：accuracy n., accurately adv., inaccurate adj.}}

{{acknowledge /əkˈnɒlɪdʒ/}}{{v. 承认；感谢；确认收到。搭配：acknowledge doing（承认做某事）。例句：He acknowledged that the plan had failed.（他承认计划失败了。）派生：acknowledgement n.}}

{{acquire /əˈkwaɪə/}}{{v. 获得；学到。搭配：acquire knowledge/skills（获得知识/技能）。例句：She acquired a taste for classical music.（她培养了对古典音乐的爱好。）派生：acquisition n.}}

{{adapt /əˈdæpt/}}{{v. 适应；改编。搭配：adapt to（适应）, adapt...from（根据…改编）。例句：It takes time to adapt to a new culture.（适应新文化需要时间。）派生：adaptation n., adaptable adj.}}

{{adequate /ˈædɪkwət/}}{{adj. 充足的；适当的。搭配：be adequate for（对…足够）。例句：The funding is adequate for the research project.（资金对研究项目来说足够了。）派生：adequacy n., inadequacy n., inadequate adj.}}

{{adjust /əˈdʒʌst/}}{{v. 调整；适应。搭配：adjust to（适应）, adjust oneself to（使自己适应）。例句：You need to adjust your strategy.（你需要调整策略。）派生：adjustment n., adjustable adj.}}

{{adopt /əˈdɒpt/}}{{v. 采纳；收养。搭配：adopt a method/policy（采纳方法/政策）。例句：The company adopted a flexible working schedule.（公司采用了弹性工作制。）派生：adoption n.}}

{{advocate /ˈædvəkeɪt/}}{{v. 提倡。n. 提倡者。搭配：advocate doing（提倡做某事）。例句：She advocates equal rights for women.（她提倡女性平等权利。）派生：advocacy n.}}

{{afford /əˈfɔːd/}}{{v. 买得起；承担得起。搭配：can't afford to do（负担不起做某事）。例句：We can't afford to waste time.（我们浪费不起时间。）派生：affordable adj.}}

{{allocate /ˈæləkeɪt/}}{{v. 分配；拨出。搭配：allocate...to（把…分配给）。例句：The government allocated funds for education.（政府拨出教育经费。）派生：allocation n.}}

{{alternative /ɔːlˈtɜːnətɪv/}}{{adj. 替代的。n. 替代品。搭配：have no alternative but to do（别无选择只能做）。例句：We need to find an alternative energy source.（我们需要找到替代能源。）派生：alternatively adv.}}

{{ambitious /æmˈbɪʃəs/}}{{adj. 有抱负的。搭配：be ambitious to do（有志于做）。例句：He is ambitious to become a scientist.（他立志成为科学家。）派生：ambition n.}}

{{analyze /ˈænəlaɪz/}}{{v. 分析。搭配：analyze data/results（分析数据/结果）。例句：Scientists analyzed the samples in the lab.（科学家在实验室分析了样本。）派生：analysis n., analyst n., analytical adj.}}

{{anticipate /ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/}}{{v. 预料；期望。搭配：anticipate doing（期望做某事）。例句：We anticipate a positive result.（我们预期会有好结果。）派生：anticipation n.}}

{{apparent /əˈpærənt/}}{{adj. 明显的；表面上的。搭配：it is apparent that（很明显…）。例句：It was apparent that she was nervous.（很明显她很紧张。）派生：apparently adv.}}

{{appeal /əˈpiːl/}}{{v. 呼吁；吸引；上诉。搭配：appeal to（呼吁；吸引）。例句：The design appeals to young consumers.（设计吸引年轻消费者。）派生：appealing adj.}}

{{appreciate /əˈpriːʃieɪt/}}{{v. 感激；欣赏。搭配：I would appreciate it if（如果…我将不胜感激）。例句：I appreciate your patience and understanding.（感谢你的耐心和理解。）派生：appreciation n., appreciative adj.}}

{{approach /əˈprəʊtʃ/}}{{v. 接近。n. 方法。搭配：approach to（…的方法）。例句：We need a new approach to education.（我们需要新的教育方法。）派生：approachable adj.}}

{{appropriate /əˈprəʊpriət/}}{{adj. 适当的。搭配：be appropriate for（适合于）。例句：Please wear appropriate clothing.（请穿着得体。）派生：appropriately adv., inappropriate adj.}}

{{arise /əˈraɪz/}}{{v. 出现；产生。搭配：arise from/out of（由…引起）。例句：Problems may arise from the new policy.（新政策可能引发问题。）辨析：arise vi. / rise vi. / raise vt.}}

{{assess /əˈses/}}{{v. 评估。搭配：assess the situation（评估情况）。例句：Teachers assess students through various methods.（教师通过多种方式评估学生。）派生：assessment n.}}

{{assign /əˈsaɪn/}}{{v. 分配；指派。搭配：assign sb. sth.（分配某人某事）。例句：The teacher assigned homework to the class.（老师给全班布置了作业。）派生：assignment n.}}

{{associate /əˈsəʊʃieɪt/}}{{v. 联系。搭配：associate...with（把…与…联系起来）。例句：People associate the color white with purity.（人们把白色与纯洁联系在一起。）派生：association n.}}

{{assume /əˈsjuːm/}}{{v. 假设；承担。搭配：assume responsibility（承担责任）。例句：Don't assume anything without evidence.（没有证据不要假设任何事情。）派生：assumption n.}}

{{attach /əˈtætʃ/}}{{v. 附上；重视。搭配：attach importance to（重视）。例句：The school attaches great importance to discipline.（学校非常重视纪律。）派生：attachment n.}}

{{attempt /əˈtempt/}}{{v./n. 尝试。搭配：attempt to do（尝试做某事）。例句：He attempted to solve the problem but failed.（他试图解决问题但失败了。）派生：attempted adj.}}

{{available /əˈveɪləbl/}}{{adj. 可获得的；有空的。搭配：be available to/for（可供…使用）。例句：Tickets are available online.（可在网上购票。）派生：availability n., unavailable adj.}}

{{aware /əˈweə/}}{{adj. 意识到的。搭配：be aware of（意识到）。例句：Are you aware of the risks?（你意识到风险了吗？）派生：awareness n., unaware adj.}}

{{benefit /ˈbenɪfɪt/}}{{n. 利益。v. 使受益。搭配：benefit from（从…受益）。例句：Everyone can benefit from reading.（每个人都能从阅读中受益。）派生：beneficial adj.}}

{{budget /ˈbʌdʒɪt/}}{{n. 预算。搭配：on a budget（节约地）, budget for（为…做预算）。例句：We need to stay within budget.（我们需要在预算范围内。）派生：budgetary adj.}}

{{campaign /kæmˈpeɪn/}}{{n. 运动；战役。搭配：launch a campaign（发起运动）。例句：The government launched a campaign against pollution.（政府发起了治污运动。）派生：campaigner n.}}

{{candidate /ˈkændɪdət/}}{{n. 候选人。搭配：candidate for（…的候选人）。例句：There are five candidates for the position.（这个职位有五位候选人。）派生：candidacy n.}}

{{capable /ˈkeɪpəbl/}}{{adj. 有能力的。搭配：be capable of doing（有能力做某事）。例句：She is capable of leading the team.（她有能力领导团队。）派生：capability n., incapable adj.}}

{{circumstance /ˈsɜːkəmstəns/}}{{n. 情况。搭配：under no circumstances（决不）。例句：Under no circumstances should you give up.（在任何情况下都不应放弃。）注意：置于句首时部分倒装。}}

{{commit /kəˈmɪt/}}{{v. 犯（罪）；承诺。搭配：commit oneself to（致力于）。例句：He committed himself to protecting the environment.（他致力于保护环境。）派生：commitment n.}}

{{communicate /kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt/}}{{v. 交流；传达。搭配：communicate with（与…交流）。例句：Good leaders communicate effectively with their team.（好的领导者与团队有效沟通。）派生：communication n.}}

{{compete /kəmˈpiːt/}}{{v. 竞争；比赛。搭配：compete with/against（与…竞争）。例句：Athletes compete for gold medals.（运动员争夺金牌。）派生：competition n., competitive n., competitor n.}}

{{concentrate /ˈkɒnsəntreɪt/}}{{v. 集中；专注。搭配：concentrate on（专注于）。例句：Concentrate on your studies and you will succeed.（专注于学习，你会成功的。）派生：concentration n.}}

{{conclude /kənˈkluːd/}}{{v. 得出结论；结束。搭配：conclude that（得出结论…）。例句：The study concluded that exercise is beneficial.（研究得出结论：锻炼有益。）派生：conclusion n.}}

{{confirm /kənˈfɜːm/}}{{v. 确认；证实。搭配：confirm a reservation（确认预订）。例句：Please confirm your attendance by Friday.（请在周五前确认出席。）派生：confirmation n.}}

{{confuse /kənˈfjuːz/}}{{v. 使困惑；混淆。搭配：be confused about（对…困惑）。例句：The instructions confused me.（说明把我弄糊涂了。）派生：confusion n., confusing adj., confused adj.}}

{{conscious /ˈkɒnʃəs/}}{{adj. 有意识的。搭配：be conscious of（意识到）。例句：She was conscious of the need to change.（她意识到需要改变。）派生：consciousness n., unconscious adj., subconscious adj.}}

{{consequence /ˈkɒnsɪkwəns/}}{{n. 结果；后果。搭配：as a consequence（因此）, face the consequences（面对后果）。例句：You must face the consequences of your actions.（你必须面对你行为的后果。）派生：consequently adv.}}

{{contribute /kənˈtrɪbjuːt/}}{{v. 贡献；导致。搭配：contribute to（有助于；导致）。例句：Everyone should contribute to society.（每个人都应为社会做贡献。）派生：contribution n.}}

{{convince /kənˈvɪns/}}{{v. 使确信；说服。搭配：convince sb. of（使某人确信）。例句：He convinced me of the importance of education.（他使我相信了教育的重要性。）派生：conviction n., convincing adj.}}

{{cooperate /kəʊˈɒpəreɪt/}}{{v. 合作。搭配：cooperate with（与…合作）。例句：The two teams cooperated on the project.（两个团队在项目上合作。）派生：cooperation n., cooperative adj.}}

{{cope /kəʊp/}}{{v. 应对。搭配：cope with（应对）。例句：She learned to cope with stress.（她学会了应对压力。）注意：cope是不及物动词。}}

{{create /kriˈeɪt/}}{{v. 创造；创建。搭配：create opportunities（创造机会）。例句：Technology has created new possibilities.（技术创造了新的可能性。）派生：creation n., creative adj., creativity n.}}

{{critical /ˈkrɪtɪkl/}}{{adj. 批评的；关键的；危急的。搭配：be critical to/for（对…至关重要）。例句：Critical thinking is essential for students.（批判性思维对学生至关重要。）派生：criticism n., criticize v., critically adv.}}

{{crucial /ˈkruːʃəl/}}{{adj. 至关重要的。搭配：play a crucial role in（在…中起关键作用）。例句：Education plays a crucial role in personal development.（教育在个人发展中起关键作用。）近义词：vital, essential, critical。}}

{{decline /dɪˈklaɪn/}}{{v./n. 下降；拒绝。搭配：in decline（在下降中）。例句：The number of wild animals has declined sharply.（野生动物数量急剧下降。）近义词：decrease, fall, refuse。}}

{{demonstrate /ˈdemənstreɪt/}}{{v. 证明；演示。搭配：demonstrate that（证明…）。例句：The results demonstrate the effectiveness of the method.（结果证明了方法的有效性。）派生：demonstration n.}}

{{deserve /dɪˈzɜːv/}}{{v. 值得；应得。搭配：deserve to do（值得做某事）。例句：You deserve a rest after all that hard work.（辛苦工作后你值得休息。）派生：deserved adj., deserving adj.}}

{{determine /dɪˈtɜːmɪn/}}{{v. 决定；确定。搭配：be determined to do（决心做某事）。例句：She is determined to succeed.（她决心成功。）派生：determination n., determined adj.}}

{{devote /dɪˈvəʊt/}}{{v. 致力于。搭配：devote...to（把…奉献给）。例句：He devoted his life to science.（他一生致力于科学。）派生：devotion n., devoted adj.}}

{{distinguish /dɪˈstɪŋɡwɪʃ/}}{{v. 区分。搭配：distinguish...from（把…与…区分开）。例句：It's hard to distinguish fact from fiction.（很难区分事实和虚构。）派生：distinguished adj., distinction n.}}

{{distribute /dɪˈstrɪbjuːt/}}{{v. 分配；分发。搭配：distribute...to（把…分发给）。例句：Food was distributed to the flood victims.（食物被分发给洪水灾民。）派生：distribution n.}}

{{dominate /ˈdɒmɪneɪt/}}{{v. 支配；占主导地位。搭配：dominate the market（主导市场）。例句：The company dominates the technology sector.（公司主导着技术领域。）派生：dominance n., dominant adj.}}

{{eliminate /ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt/}}{{v. 消除；淘汰。搭配：eliminate...from（从…中消除）。例句：We must eliminate all sources of pollution.（我们必须消除所有污染源。）派生：elimination n.}}

{{embrace /ɪmˈbreɪs/}}{{v. 拥抱；接受。搭配：embrace change（拥抱变化）。例句：We should embrace new ideas.（我们应该接受新思想。）近义词：accept, welcome。}}

{{emerge /ɪˈmɜːdʒ/}}{{v. 出现。搭配：emerge from（从…中出现）。例句：New leaders emerged during the crisis.（危机中涌现了新领袖。）派生：emergence n., emerging adj., emergency n.}}

{{emphasize /ˈemfəsaɪz/}}{{v. 强调。搭配：emphasize the importance of（强调…的重要性）。例句：The teacher emphasized the need for hard work.（老师强调了努力学习的必要性。）派生：emphasis n., emphatic adj.}}

{{enable /ɪˈneɪbl/}}{{v. 使能够。搭配：enable sb. to do（使某人能够做）。例句：Technology enables us to work from home.（技术使我们能够在家中工作。）反义词：disable。}}

{{encounter /ɪnˈkaʊntə/}}{{v./n. 遇到。搭配：encounter difficulties（遇到困难）。例句：We may encounter unexpected challenges.（我们可能遇到意想不到的挑战。）近义词：meet, come across。}}

{{enhance /ɪnˈhɑːns/}}{{v. 增强；提高。搭配：enhance quality（提高质量）。例句：Exercise enhances both physical and mental health.（锻炼增强身心健康。）派生：enhancement n.}}

{{ensure /ɪnˈʃʊə/}}{{v. 确保。搭配：ensure that（确保…）。例句：Please ensure that all doors are locked.（请确保所有门都锁好了。）辨析：ensure vs assure vs insure。}}

{{establish /ɪˈstæblɪʃ/}}{{v. 建立。搭配：establish a relationship（建立关系）。例句：The school was established in 1950.（学校建于1950年。）派生：establishment n.}}

{{evaluate /ɪˈvæljueɪt/}}{{v. 评估。搭配：evaluate the results（评估结果）。例句：We need to evaluate the effectiveness of the program.（我们需要评估项目的效果。）派生：evaluation n.}}

{{evolve /ɪˈvɒlv/}}{{v. 进化；发展。搭配：evolve into（进化成）。例句：Languages evolve over time.（语言随时间演变。）派生：evolution n., evolutionary adj.}}

{{expand /ɪkˈspænd/}}{{v. 扩大。搭配：expand the business（扩大业务）。例句：The company plans to expand overseas.（公司计划向海外扩展。）派生：expansion n.}}

{{expose /ɪkˈspəʊz/}}{{v. 暴露；揭露。搭配：be exposed to（暴露于；接触）。例句：Children should be exposed to different cultures.（孩子应该接触不同文化。）派生：exposure n.}}

{{extend /ɪkˈstend/}}{{v. 延伸；延长。搭配：extend the deadline（延长截止日期）。例句：They extended the deadline by one week.（他们把截止日期延长了一周。）派生：extension n., extensive adj.}}

{{facilitate /fəˈsɪlɪteɪt/}}{{v. 促进；使便利。搭配：facilitate communication（促进交流）。例句：Technology facilitates learning.（技术促进学习。）派生：facility n., facilitator n.}}

{{generate /ˈdʒenəreɪt/}}{{v. 产生；引起。搭配：generate electricity/income（发电/产生收入）。例句：Solar panels generate clean energy.（太阳能电池板产生清洁能源。）派生：generation n., generator n.}}

{{guarantee /ˌɡærənˈtiː/}}{{v./n. 保证。搭配：guarantee that（保证…）。例句：Hard work guarantees success.（努力工作保证成功。）近义词：ensure, promise。}}
